- **Mean Reciprocal Rank (MRR)** : it gives a measure of the average ranking of the first buggy UI screen/component in the candidate list given by a model. It is calculated as: _𝑀𝑅𝑅_ = _𝑁_ [1]  - _𝑖𝑁_ =1 _𝑟𝑎𝑛𝑘_ 1 _𝑖_ [,]

for _𝑁_ queries ( _𝑟𝑎𝑛𝑘𝑖_ is the rank of the first buggy UI screen/component for query _𝑖_ ).

- **Mean Average Precision (MAP)** : it gives a measure of the
average ranking of all the buggy UI screens/components for a
query. It is computed as: _𝑀𝐴𝑃_ = _𝑁_ 1  - _𝑖𝑁_ =1 _𝐵𝑈_ 1  - _𝑏𝐵𝑈_ =1 _[𝑃][𝑖]_ [(] _[𝑟𝑎𝑛𝑘][𝑏]_ [)][,]
where _𝐵𝑈_ is the set buggy UI screens/components for query _𝑖_,
_𝑟𝑎𝑛𝑘𝑏_ is the rank of the buggy UI screen/component _𝑏_, and
_𝑃𝑖_ ( _𝑘_ ) = _[𝑏𝑢𝑔𝑔𝑦]_ [_] _[𝑒𝑙𝑒𝑚𝑒𝑛𝑡𝑠]_ _𝑘_ is the number of buggy UI screens/com
ponents in the top- _𝑘_ candidates.

- **Hits@K (H@K)** : it is the percentage of queries for which a
buggy UI screen/component is retrieved in the top-K candidates.


